```txt
Title: 🧠 P1: Implement arena allocator for contiguous weight storage

Priority: P1 (High - affects performance scaling)
Type: Performance/Architecture
Assignee: @you
Due: 7 days
Labels: p1, high, performance, memory, architecture

Description:
Architectural review identified pointer chasing in current struct design.
Implement single-contiguous-memory allocator to improve cache locality.

Current Problem:
- Layer structs contain pointers to other pointers
- Causes cache prediction failures (cache misses)
- Memory fragmentation from multiple mallocs
- Poor memory locality for embedded systems

Solution:
Implement arena allocator where all model weights live in one contiguous memory block.

Technical Spec:
```c
// Arena allocator design
typedef struct {
    float* arena;           // Single malloc for ALL weights
    size_t capacity;        // Total bytes allocated
    size_t used;            // Bytes currently used
    uint32_t magic;         // Validation magic number
    uint32_t version;       // Arena layout version
} TransformerArena;

// Functions
TransformerArena* arena_create(size_t size);
void* arena_alloc(TransformerArena* arena, size_t size);
void arena_reset(TransformerArena* arena);
void arena_destroy(TransformerArena* arena);
```

Implementation Tasks:

· Create include/allocator.h with arena interface
· Implement src/allocator.c with arena functions
· Convert model loading to use arena in src/model.c
· Update backpropagation to work with arena offsets
· Benchmark cache misses: perf stat -e cache-misses
· Document in docs/MEMORY_LAYOUT.md

Files:

· src/allocator.c
· include/allocator.h
· src/model.c (modify)
· tests/test_allocator.c
· docs/MEMORY_LAYOUT.md

Acceptance Criteria:

· Single malloc for entire model weights
· 20%+ reduction in cache misses measured
· All tests pass
· Memory footprint identical or better
· No performance regression

Notes:
Essential for embedded deployment where cache efficiency is critical.

```

